{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1969","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Shifts and Sorting"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cyclic shift"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of some string $$$s$$$ as a transformation from $$$s_1 s_2 \\dots s_{n-1} s_{n}$$$ into $$$s_{n} s_1 s_2 \\dots s_{n-1}$$$. In other words, you take one last character $$$s_n$$$ and place it before the first character while moving all other characters to the right."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a binary string $$$s$$$ (a string consisting of only "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-s and/or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-s)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation, you can choose any substring $$$s_l s_{l+1} \\dots s_r$$$ ($$$1 \\le l \\lt r \\le |s|$$$) and cyclically shift it. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cost"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of such operation is equal to $$$r - l + 1$$$ (or the length of the chosen substring)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can perform the given operation any number of times. What is the minimum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"total"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cost to make $$$s$$$ sorted in non-descending order?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each test case contains a binary string $$$s$$$ ($$$2 \\le |s| \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$s_i \\in$$$ {"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"}) — the string you need to sort."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Additional constraint on the input: the sum of lengths of strings over all test cases doesn't exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the single integer — the minimum total cost to make string sorted using operation above any number of times."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n10\n0000\n11000\n101011\n01101001\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n0\n9\n5\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, you can choose the whole string and perform a cyclic shift: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The length of the substring is $$$2$$$, so the cost is $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the string is already sorted, so you don't need to perform any operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, one of the optimal strategies is the next: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose substring $$$[1, 3]$$$: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose substring $$$[2, 4]$$$: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00110"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose substring $$$[3, 5]$$$: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00110"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" The total cost is $$$3 + 3 + 3 = 9$$$."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1969B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1969/problem/B"}